- local variables in small scopes do not need long names
- a short comment is usually better than a long name: it gives more info, and yet doesn't repeat a sentence-long name (which still doesn't convey what was needed in the first place) over and over

```suggestion
  // Match all (non-floating) windows in the tabpage, including hidden / non-focusable.
  bool all = cmdarg != NULL && cmdarg->cmdidx != CMD_quit;
